SUMMARY:Shining Rock via Shining Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nShining Rock via Shining Creek and
  Old Butt Knob trails.\nApproximately 8.5 miles\, 2\,700' elevation gain\n
 Pace approximately 2-2.5mph average\n\nI have not been on the Shining Cree
 k trail since it was damaged by Tropical Storm Fred in 2021. Last year the
  trail was rehabbed by the Forest Service and I figure it's time to check 
 it out.\n\nThe hike should be challenging. We'll start on the Shining Cree
 k trail and soon turn on to the Old Butt Knob trail. On the Old Butt Knob 
 trail we will work our way up steeply to the peak of Shining Rock. We'll l
 unch on Shining Rock\, head over to the Art Loeb trail and then back down 
 the Shining Creek trail and back to the cars.\n\nWe'll meet at 8:45 at the
  Pisgah Ranger Station for a 9:00 sharp departure. Of you can meet us at t
 he trailhead (35°21'57.6"N 82°49'05.3"W) on US 276 for a 9:30 start.\n\n
 This hike is in the Shining Rock Wilderness so the group size is set by la
 w to a maximum of 10.\n\nDogs are welcome\, I will have my dog with me.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314249717
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260412T185603Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260412T185603Z
